Wine ARM64EC: fix the stubless-client varargs argument window in rpcrt4.

The ARM64EC thunks for NdrClientCall2 / NdrClientCall3 / NdrAsyncClientCall built
the NDR argument array from x4, assuming x4 points at the first stack argument.
That is wrong in practice: only the two arguments the thunk spills itself (x2/x3)
land in the right place, so any RPC procedure with three or more parameters reads
the caller's frame instead of its arguments. The Service Control Manager client in
sechost.dll hits this on every call -- ROpenSCManagerW's 4th parameter is an [out]
context handle, so NdrContextHandleUnmarshall receives a garbage pointer (observed:
0x10) and faults writing to it. That is the arm64ec-only "sc start fails / msiexec
StopServices crashes / EABackgroundService dies" bug.

ARM64EC mirrors the x64 stack layout: at entry sp points at the 32-byte home area,
so the home slots for x2/x3 are at sp+0x10 / sp+0x18 and the first stack argument
follows contiguously at sp+0x20. Spilling into the home slots and pointing the NDR
stack there reproduces exactly what the x86_64 thunk does, and needs no x4.

--- a/dlls/rpcrt4/ndr_stubless.c
+++ b/dlls/rpcrt4/ndr_stubless.c
@@ NdrClientCall2 (arm64ec)
-         "stp x2, x3, [x4, #-0x10]!\n\t"
-         "mov x2, x4\n\t"          /* stack */
+         "stp x2, x3, [sp, #0x30]\n\t"
+         "add x2, sp, #0x30\n\t"   /* stack */
@@ NdrAsyncClientCall (arm64ec)
-         "stp x2, x3, [x4, #-0x10]!\n\t"
-         "mov x2, x4\n\t"          /* stack */
+         "stp x2, x3, [sp, #0x30]\n\t"
+         "add x2, sp, #0x30\n\t"   /* stack */
@@ NdrClientCall3 / Ndr64AsyncClientCall (arm64ec)
-         "str x3, [x4, #-0x8]!\n\t"
-         "mov x3, x4\n\t"          /* stack */
+         "str x3, [sp, #0x38]\n\t"
+         "add x3, sp, #0x38\n\t"   /* stack */

(sp+0x30 / sp+0x38 account for the thunk's own "stp x29, x30, [sp, #-0x20]!"
prologue: orig_sp = sp + 0x20, so orig_sp+0x10 = sp+0x30.)

STATUS (2026-09-07)
-------------------
Verified on device: winecfg on arm64ec goes from 152 rpcrt4+0x64AA4 access
violations to 0 with this patch, and EABackgroundService.exe no longer
generates a crash report. Native ARM64EC RPC callers are fixed.

KNOWN REMAINING GAP: emulated x64 callers (a Windows x64 exe running under FEX
inside an arm64ec container) still get a wrong argument window - the block reads
as all zeros, so an [out] IsSimpleRef parameter comes through NULL and
client_do_args raises RPC_X_NULL_REF_POINTER, surfacing as error 487
(ERROR_INVALID_ADDRESS). Neither x4 (pre-patch) nor sp+0x20 (this patch) locates
the arguments for that caller. These entry points are declared "@ varargs" in
rpcrt4.spec and are __attribute__((naked)) asm, so the x64 -> ARM64EC entry thunk
is the suspect: it does not appear to marshal variadic stack arguments. That is
the next thing to fix.
